@startuml 07-proposed-ingestion
!include _style.puml
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #1e293b
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #e2e8f0
  StereotypeFontColor #c4b5fd
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #334155
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #e2e8f0
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #16233b
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #93c5fd
}
skinparam queue {
  BackgroundColor #334155
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #e2e8f0
}
title **PROPOSED — Engineering Data Ingestion (ADR-005)**\nNot implemented. One neutral baseline, many sources of differing fidelity.

rectangle "Sources" {
  component "Navisworks NWD" as NWD #7f1d1d
  component "Navisworks\nproperty export\nCSV / XLSX" as NVC
  component "PCF\n(Piping Component File)\nplain text" as PCF #14532d
  component "MTO / Line list\nXLSX" as XLS
  component "IFC4\n<<phase 5>>" as IFC
  component "Manual entry" as MAN
}

note bottom of NWD
  **CANNOT BE PARSED.**
  Proprietary, Windows-only, spec not public.
  Navisworks exports only DWF/FBX/KML -
  geometry without properties.
  Freedom cannot export at all.

  So the model owner exports a property
  schedule from Manage; we ingest that.
  Never promise "upload the NWD".
end note

note bottom of PCF
  **The sleeper.** Plain text, ISOGEN's own
  input format, written by Plant 3D, CADWorx,
  AVEVA, CAESAR II, Cadmatic.

  Gives per line: every component, bore,
  item code, end-point coordinates, weight.
  An MTO nobody typed - and it needs no
  library, no licence, no Windows.
end note

rectangle "Ingestion spine (new)" {
  component "ImportProfile\n<<column map, per project>>" as PROF
  component "Parser\n(openspout / text)" as PARSE
  queue "Queued batch job\n<<jobs, job_batches\nalready migrated>>" as JOB
  database "import_batches\n+ import_rows\n<<staged, hashed>>" as STAGE
  component "Preview + diff\n1204 new / 87 changed\n3 removed / 12 errors" as PREV
}

database "**engineering_items**\nTHE BASELINE\n--\ntag, size, spec, qty\nsource_kind, confidence\nimport_batch_id\nsubsystem_id / facility_id" as BASE #1e3a5f

database "line_list_entries\n<<design envelope>>" as LL
database "pms_specs\n+ pms_spec_items" as PMS

rectangle "Existing, reused unchanged" {
  database "documents\n<<CDE>>\nisometrics, support dwgs" as CDE
  database "subsystems\n<<ADR-004>>" as SS
  database "purchase_order_items\nmaterial_lots" as PROC
}

rectangle "What it unlocks" {
  component "Shortage =\n**MTO** - delivered" as U1
  component "Progress =\ninstalled / baseline" as U2
  component "PMS compliance\n<<advisory>>" as U3
  component "Rev B -> Rev C diff" as U4
}

NWD -[#ef4444,dashed]-> NVC : export from Manage
NVC --> PARSE
PCF --> PARSE
XLS --> PARSE
IFC ..> PARSE
MAN --> BASE

PROF --> PARSE
PARSE --> JOB
JOB --> STAGE
STAGE --> PREV
PREV --> BASE : COMMIT\n<<one transaction>>
PREV -[#ef4444]-> STAGE : REJECT

BASE --> LL
BASE ..> PMS : validated against
BASE --> SS : scoped to
CDE <.. BASE : source_document_id\n+ revision

BASE --> U1
BASE --> U2
PMS --> U3
STAGE --> U4
U1 --> PROC

note right of BASE
  **One baseline, many sources.**
  A line list, an MTO and a PCF parse are three
  statements about the same physical reality,
  arriving at different times with different
  authority.

  Give each its own table and "how much 6in pipe
  does SS-6601 need?" has three answers and no
  way to choose.

  So every row records **where it came from**.
  When sources disagree the system does not pick
  a winner - it raises a reconciliation item,
  because on a real project that disagreement
  IS the finding. It usually means the iso was
  revised and the MTO was not re-issued.
end note

note right of STAGE
  **Versioned, immutable, hashed.**
  Import is never truncate-and-reload: that
  would silently delete the baseline a PO was
  raised against.

  Keeping batches gives the Rev B -> Rev C diff
  for free - probably the single report most
  likely to sell the product - plus "which
  revision did we buy against", and a safe
  rollback.

  file_hash makes re-upload idempotent.
end note

note bottom of PREV
  A 40,000-row MTO that fails on row 39,999 must
  not leave 39,998 rows behind. Same two-stage
  commitment as the MR approval flow: a human
  sees what will happen before it happens.
end note

@enduml
